# .cursorrules

model_routing:

- when: "Scaffolding new code (Next.js pages, Supabase queries, shadcn/ui components, Clerk auth flows)"
  prefer: "gpt-5-codex"

- when: "Day-to-day coding that also requires reasoning (multi-step API integrations, Supabase Edge Functions, complex joins, wiring Clerk + Supabase)"
  prefer: "o3-pro"

- when: "Debugging or reasoning-heavy problems (RLS policies, schema design, auth role logic, migrations, performance tuning)"
  prefer: "claude-4.1-opus-thinking"

- when: "Repo-wide analysis (verifying schema ↔ Prisma ↔ migrations consistency, auditing full RLS policies, checking cross-file dependencies)"
  prefer: "claude-4-sonnet-max"

- when: "Quick drafts, boilerplate, documentation, or scratchpad tasks where speed > precision"
  prefer: "gpt-5-codex"

Notes:

- Default daily driver: o3-pro (balanced code + reasoning).
- Switch to gpt-5-codex for clean scaffolds or repetitive coding.
- Use claude-4.1-opus-thinking for logic-heavy debugging, schema analysis, migrations, or architectural Q&A.
- Use claude-4-sonnet-max for full-repo audits or ingestion of many files.
- Fall back to gpt-5-codex.
